# Every Home Base model call gets a fresh decision and audit record
#
# Fixes: Odysseus could return an in-memory response before the permission
# layer saw the request. The cache key used configured endpoint headers;
# Home Base's per-request user identity was added only at HTTP send time.
# Why: partitioning by user would still skip policy changes and receipts
# for repeated requests by the same person. Disable both reads and writes
# whenever HOME_BASE_PERMISSION_LAYER_HOST is present, including anonymous
# calls, aliases, IP addresses, and incomplete configuration. Home Base
# routes all model requests through its broker. Without that variable,
# upstream cache behavior stays unchanged. No new setting is needed.
# Upstream: a Home Base integration feature. Depends on 0005 and 0006.
# Test: tests/test_home_base_response_cache.py

